avengers infinity war proved that it  takes quite a lot to make thanos cry  usually marvel's massive purple titan is  as strong on the inside as he appears on  the outside  especially when it comes to causing  serious mayhem after all he was already  proudly decimating half the existing  population in the universe one planet at  a time  before acquiring the infinity stones and  powering up the infinity gauntlet which  offered him greater efficiency in  achieving his goal  a simple snap of his fingers at the end  of avengers infinity war in the universe  was only half as full of living things  as it was the moment before  and thanos couldn't have been happier  about it he even sacrificed one of his  adoptive daughters gamora to get his  hands on the soul stone  which requires the seeker to offer up  the thing they love most in the world as  a sacrifice before acquiring it  though thanos is undeniably a genocidal  maniac with skewed morals the human who  brought him to life on the big screen is  thankfully the complete opposite  sure he's muscular and strong with a  booming voice but thanos actor josh  brolin is quite soft at heart  in fact brolin previously confessed that  he had complicated feelings about a  scene in which thanos kills one of his  many victims  feeling bad for both the character and  the actor on the receiving end of thanos  ruthlessness  and no despite the fact that killing  gamora made his character thanos cry  that's not the one he was talking about  what did it cost  [Music]  everything in a july 2018 interview with  usa today  brolin identified the avengers infinity  war scene in which thanos brutally kills  loki played by tom hiddleston as a scene  he didn't totally enjoy filming  the moment happens very early on in the  movie when thanos and his pack a black  order henchmen intercept the grandmaster  spaceship that's carrying loki  thor heimdall the hulk and the other  asgardians who became refugees after  surter destroyed asgard at the end of  thor ragnarok  loki offers to be thanos and company's  guide when they eventually touch down on  earth but he's actually deceiving him  hoping to get close enough to thanos so  he can stab and kill him  this backfires and thanos uses the space  stone inside the infinity gauntlet to  freeze loki's arm in mid-air  with one hand thanos smacks loki's knife  to the ground and with the other  chokes and kills him roland knew this is  what had to be done for the story but  that doesn't mean he was all smiles and  laughter throughout filming to this  particular scene  the actor felt especially bad for tom  hiddleston who had at that point been  playing loki in the mcu for the better  part of a decade  roland told usa today he had been with  that character for so long and he was so  lauded for doing it  so choking him out wasn't the most fun  thing i had ever done  while brolin didn't have any fun and  effectively taking away one of  hiddleston's most popular roles he did  find pleasure in the backlash it caused  the actor added that on instagram people  are saying things like i hate you  that's fantastic i'm like the one guy  who smiles when he sees that  it's like it worked brolin later  revealed in the same interview that he  also took pleasure in a different aspect  of the very same scene  thanos beating the hulk in a one-on-one  fist fight which he found rather  satisfying  roland said i love that thanos uses a  knee that was great  the good news after the fact is that  avengers infinity war isn't the last  fans get to see of loki  the god of mischief albeit a version of  the character who didn't die and instead  escaped with the space stone during the  avengers time heist and end game will  star in his very own series on disney  plus set to premiere on july 11  2021 hopefully this happy ending makes  brolin feel a little bit better about  the last scene he shared with hiddleston  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your